  pairLookup02_provenance_unsealed
  ================================

  WHAT IT IS.  Witness of the PROVENANCE LINE every lookup card carries (DEV.md
  4c C227 (a), the architect's ruling).  The lookups read the INSTALLATION
  catalogue by design -- their subject is the catalogue -- so each card, and
  the `catalogue` object of the result JSON, names the source, the
  installation's catalogue release (data/standards/CATALOGUE.dat) and the
  case's seal state.

  THIS CASE: UNSEALED (no constant/propertyManifest).  The card reads
  `case unsealed`; there is no sealed release it could differ from.  Its
  sibling pairLookup03_provenance_stale_seal is sealed from an older release
  and the line says `differs`.  Pinned: the tier word, the card bytes.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
